<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dilwara Temples</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dilwara Temples are a group of five Jain temples at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, famed for their intricately carved white marble interiors. The oldest, the Vimal Vasahi dedicated to Rishabhanatha, was built in 1031 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vimal-shah">Vimala</a>, a minister of the Chaulukya king Bhima I, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luna-vasahi">Luna Vasahi</a> was added in 1230 by the brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vastupala">Vastupala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tejapala">Tejapala</a>.</p></div>
